WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Type III covers low-pressure chillers. These are commercial systems — big
equipment, big consequences.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
A purge unit removes air and non-condensable gases that leak into low-pressure
systems. Since the system operates below atmospheric pressure air constantly
tries to enter through any imperfection in seals, gaskets, or joints. The purge

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
Purge Unit: Removes air and non-condensables that leak into low-pressure
systems.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Monitoring purge unit run time is a key
maintenance indicator for chiller health.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: High purge run time means excessive air leaks. And — Air in
the system raises head pressure and reduces efficiency

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
Why does a low-pressure system have air leaking in rather than refrigerant
leaking out? Think about the pressure relationship.

